-# VPnBot exact active VLESS and Trojan revocation
+# VPnBot exact active user revocation
 
 This fork carries one deliberately narrow behavior change for VPnBot-managed
-VLESS and Trojan users: a successful `HandlerService.RemoveUser` operation both
-removes the credential from the in-memory validator and interrupts the active
-transport connections authenticated as that exact inbound email.
+VLESS, Trojan, VMess and Shadowsocks users: a successful
+`HandlerService.RemoveUser` operation both removes the credential from the
+in-memory validator and interrupts the active transport connections
+authenticated as that exact inbound email.
 
 The capability is reported by `xray version` as:
 
 ```text
-VPnBot capability: vpnbot-active-revoke-v2
+VPnBot capability: vpnbot-active-revoke-v3
 ```
 
-The version statement also retains the earlier
-`vpnbot-active-revoke-v1` marker as a backward-compatibility claim for VLESS.
-VPnBot node installers and updaters that require Trojan revocation must fail
-closed when the `v2` marker is absent.
+The version statement also retains `vpnbot-active-revoke-v1` for VLESS and
+`vpnbot-active-revoke-v2` for VLESS plus Trojan. VPnBot node installers and
+updaters that require all managed Xray protocols must fail closed when the
+`v3` marker is absent.
 
 The implementation uses one shared active-session registry primitive inside
-each VLESS and Trojan inbound handler. Registry admission and
+each VLESS, Trojan, VMess and Shadowsocks inbound handler. Registry admission and
 `AddUser`/`RemoveUser` mutations share one mutex, so a connection authenticated
 before deletion cannot register after the same email has been deleted or
 replaced. `RemoveUser` deletes the validator entry before closing its captured
@@ -31,8 +32,21 @@ user's active connection.
 
 Regression coverage lives in
 `common/active_user_sessions_test.go`,
-`proxy/vless/inbound/active_sessions_test.go`, and
-`proxy/trojan/active_sessions_test.go`. Before a VPnBot release, the fork must
-also pass the upstream protocol scenarios and an external long-stream E2E for
-every transport used by production: VLESS TCP, WebSocket, gRPC and XHTTP, plus
-Trojan TCP.
+`proxy/vless/inbound/active_sessions_test.go`, and the corresponding VLESS,
+Trojan, VMess and Shadowsocks tests. Before a VPnBot release, the fork must also
+pass the upstream protocol scenarios and an external long-stream E2E for every
+transport used by production: VLESS TCP, WebSocket, gRPC and XHTTP, plus Trojan
+TCP, VMess TCP and Shadowsocks TCP/UDP.
+
+## Single-connection live user audit
+
+The additional version marker
+`VPnBot capability: vpnbot-live-user-audit-v1` advertises the read-only
+`xray api vpnbot-audit-users` command. The command opens one local gRPC
+connection, lists every inbound, retrieves every UserManager user, verifies
+each list through `GetInboundUsersCount`, and repeats the complete pass. It
+returns both passes as typed JSON so the VPnBot node helper can reject any
+registry drift without launching a process and gRPC connection per inbound.
+
+This command does not replace or weaken the active-revoke capability. It never
+adds or removes users and never restarts Xray.
